Electrode Slag Remelting (ESR) furnace represents an advanced secondary‑refining process that improves the purity and mechanical performance of high‑value alloys such as specialty steels and superalloys. The technology melts a consumable electrode within a high‑resistance slag bath, allowing precise control of temperature and solidification while removing inclusions, dissolved gases, and other impurities. Because the slag acts as both a refining medium and a thermal buffer, the resulting ingots exhibit fine grain structures, low segregation, and superior corrosion‑resistance attributes essential for aerospace components, turbine blades, and nuclear‑grade parts.
